y=2n

Typical Uses of Python Visualizations

Python should be used to illustrate:

number sequences

geometric shapes

coordinate geometry

probability experiments

function behavior

algorithm behavior

mathematical patterns

2. Visual Discovery Principle

Whenever possible, replace purely verbal explanations with visual discovery.

Example:

Instead of stating:

Even numbers increase by 2.

Provide a visualization showing evenly spaced points on a number line.

The goal is for learners to see the pattern themselves.

3. Interactive Lessons with JavaScript

JavaScript should be used to create interactive exploration tools where learners manipulate variables and observe mathematical behavior in real time.

Recommended Technologies

Vanilla JavaScript + HTML

p5.js for visual math exploration

D3.js for data-driven visualizations

Interactive tools should allow learners to:

modify parameters

test predictions

observe emerging patterns

explore mathematical relationships

4. Structure of Interactive Components

Each interactive component should include:

Concept

Brief explanation of the mathematical idea.

Interactive Exploration

A small JavaScript program that allows learners to manipulate values.

Guided Questions

Questions encouraging exploration, such as:

What happens if you increase this value?

Can you predict the next result?

Do you notice a pattern?

5. Example Interactive Lesson
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<body>

<h3>Explore Even Numbers</h3>

<input type="range" min="1" max="20" value="1" id="slider">

<p>Result: <span id="value"></span></p>

<script>

const slider = document.getElementById("slider");
const output = document.getElementById("value");

function update() {
    let n = slider.value;
    output.innerText = 2 * n;
}

slider.addEventListener("input", update);

update();

</script>

</body>
</html>

This interactive example allows learners to explore:

2
𝑛
2n

and observe how it generates even numbers.

6. Pedagogical Principles

All illustrations and interactive elements must follow these principles:

Exploration before explanation

Visual intuition over abstraction

Immediate feedback

Encouragement of curiosity

Learners should feel that they are discovering mathematics, not simply memorizing rules.

7. When to Use Each Tool

Use Python visualizations when:

demonstrating mathematical graphs

illustrating geometry

visualizing numerical patterns

showing algorithm behavior

Use JavaScript interactive tools when:

learners should manipulate variables

exploring dynamic mathematical relationships

building intuition through experimentation

8. Integration with Lessons

When appropriate, each lesson should include:

one Python-generated illustration

one interactive JavaScript exploration

These elements should support the lesson's main concept and help learners develop mathematical intuition through visualization and experimentation.
